SUMMARY:Long Pose Figure Drawing and Painting Session
DESCRIPTION:Tuesday Night Sessions:  Sunday Edition \nSunday\, August 30\, 1 – 5 pm\, $10 per hour or $35 for the full session \n“The object isn’t to make art\, it’s to be in that wonderful state which makes art inevitable.” – Robert Henri \nThis special Sunday session is an extended version of our beloved Tuesday night figure drawing\, giving you a full four hours to sink deep into the work. Bring your favorite materials\, settle in\, listen to some good tunes in great company\, and get into your flow.  This will be a great opportunity to create a more finished work of art\, hone your portraiture skills\, or work with a material that you don’t normally get to use. \nOur model will be dressed in character (more details coming soon) and serve as our muse for the afternoon.  Whether you want to loosen up your line work\, push into a sustained study\, or simply spend a slow Sunday afternoon drawing from life\, this is your space to do it. \nYou can stay for the full session\, or drop in and pay by the hour for an hour or two. \nAll skill levels welcome\, from seasoned studio artists to total beginners. Even poets have been known to drop in. \nSunday\, August 30 | 1:00 – 5:00 pm The Space\, Montclair \nMaterials such as charcoal\, graphite\, ink\, pastels\, and paints are all welcome. Basic drawing supplies available upon request. No formal instruction is given so it is a self-guided session. \nCheck out our regular weekly Tuesday night sessions here.
